B. IRS Section 501(r) Non-Compliance (Treas. Reg. § 1.501(r)-6): The target facility is organized under IRC § 501(c)(3). The facility initiated Extraordinary Collection Actions (ECAs) / collection transfers prior to completing reasonable efforts to determine Financial Assistance Policy (FAP) eligibility within the mandatory notification windows established by Treas. Reg. § 1.501(r)-6.

C. PA FCEUA & Consumer Protection Exposure (73 P.S. § 2270.4 / 73 P.S. § 201-1): Continued collection demands during an active statutory dispute constitute deceptive practices under the Fair Credit Extension Uniformity Act, triggering per se UTPCPL liability.

3. REQUESTED ADMINISTRATIVE RELIEF
1. Direct the provider/facility to cease all collection enforcement and recall the account from third-party agencies.
2. Compel reprocessing of the claim at in-network cost-sharing levels based on the QPA.
3. Initiate an administrative audit regarding 501(r) ECA compliance and FCEUA debt collection practices.
```

