## PART 4: STATUTORY REFERENCE & CASE LAW MATRIX

| Authority / Citation | Legal Scope & Rule | Consumer Defense & Litigation Impact |
|---|---|---|
| **No Surprises Act** ($\text{45 C.F.R. Part 149}$) | Caps patient liability for emergency & ancillary care at in-network QPA rates. | Removes patient from payer-provider payment disputes; mandates Federal IDR. |
| **Treas. Reg. § 1.501(r)-6** ($\text{26 U.S.C. § 501(r)}$) | Mandates $120$-day ECA prohibition & $240$-day FAP application processing windows. | Bars non-profit hospitals from suing, garnishing, or reporting to credit bureaus prematurely. |
| **PA Contract Limitations** ($\text{42 Pa.C.S. § 5525(a)}$) | $4$-year statute of limitations on written/unwritten contracts running from default. | Absolute defense against untimely suits; **must be pleaded under Pa.R.C.P. 1030 (New Matter)**. |
| **PA Acknowledgment Doctrine** (*Huntingdon*, 659 A.2d 1054) | Common-law rule governing limitation clock restarts via payment or writing. | **Partial payment restarts 4-year clock.** Written promise restarts clock *only* if clear, unequivocal, and unconditional. |
| **PA FCEUA** ($\text{73 P.S. § 2270.4}$) | Regulates first-party creditors (hospitals) and third-party collectors. | Prohibits deceptive debt collection; violations trigger *per se* UTPCPL remedies under $\text{73 P.S. § 2270.5(a)}$. |
| **PA Wage Exemption** ($\text{42 Pa.C.S. § 8127}$) | Exempts personal wages in employer hands from ordinary debt garnishment. | Protects employee earnings from direct wage attachment in PA state courts. |
| **Tenancy by the Entireties** | Shields joint spousal real estate/property from single-spouse debts. | Protects marital homes against judgments incurred individually by one spouse. |
